      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003935
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-21T09:17:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, I like option 1. the most.\n\nI could also imagine having `--ref \u003cREF\u003e` to filter for labels that apply to the ref (only return labels where the ref matches labelType.getRefPatterns()), and have `--votable` as a boolean to filter for labels that the user can vote on. Then the caller would specify both options.\n\nSupporting `--ref \u003cREF\u003e` alone could make sense, and we could reject using `--votable` without `--ref \u003cREF\u003e`.\n\nBut I\u0027m not having a strong opinion here.",
      "parentUuid": "c6e15b6f_c35dbef8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 63,
