      },
      "lineNbr": 125,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003935
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-21T07:54:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Labels can also define for which refs they apply, see [1]. I think we should only return labels that are enabled for the requested ref (for this you would need to check against the ref against the patterns from labelType.getRefPatterns()).\n\nE.g. if a label applies only to \u0027refs/heads/main\u0027, but permissions for the label are granted on \u0027refs/heads/*\u0027 the user cannot vote on the label for \"refs/heads/stable\" although they are granted the permission (because the label doesn\u0027t apply to this branch).\n\n[1] https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/Documentation/config-labels.html#label_branch",
      "revId": "1a0848249f53addfaf85d3608d7a05ca391ab2f2",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
